# Embedded Firmware Style Guide v2.4 (Excerpt)

## Rule 1.1: Magic Numbers
Do not use literal numeric constants in logic unless they are dimensionless multipliers of 0, 1, or -1. All other values must be defined as named constants with uppercase underscores (e.g., MAX_RETRY_COUNT). Rationale: Prevents obscure hardware dependencies. Exception: Bit-shift operators (e.g., `1 << 4`) are permitted.

## Rule 1.2: Interrupt Latency
Interrupt Service Routines (ISRs) must not call blocking functions or perform dynamic memory allocation. Keep ISRs under 50 cycles where possible.

## Rule 1.3: Pointer Arithmetic
Avoid pointer arithmetic in application logic; use array indexing for clarity unless performance profiling dictates otherwise.

## Rule 1.4: Volatile Qualifiers
All memory-mapped I/O registers must be declared `volatile`. Failure to do so may cause the compiler to optimize away critical reads/writes.

