commit 8f7d2a1c: Fix pagination calculation for data grid
Author: Data Science Team <ds-team@company.com>
Date:   Mon Mar 18 14:22:45 2024 -0400

    Fixed off-by-one error in page calculation and added edge case handling.

    SPECIFIED BEHAVIOURS for calculateVisibleItems function:
    1. Takes: totalItems (int ≥ 0), itemsPerPage (int ≥ 1), currentPage (int ≥ 1)
    2. Returns object with:
       - startIndex (0-based index of first visible item, inclusive)
       - endIndex (0-based index of last visible item, inclusive)
       - totalPages (total number of pages needed)
    3. Range calculation: For page p (1-indexed), items i through j are visible where:
       i = (p-1) * itemsPerPage
       j = min(totalItems-1, p * itemsPerPage - 1)
    4. The endIndex is INCLUSIVE and MUST NOT exceed totalItems-1
    5. If totalItems == 0, returns {startIndex: 0, endIndex: -1, totalPages: 1}
    6. Example: totalItems=25, itemsPerPage=10, currentPage=2
       Expected: startIndex=10, endIndex=19, totalPages=3
    7. Example: totalItems=25, itemsPerPage=10, currentPage=3  // Last page partial
       Expected: startIndex=20, endIndex=24, totalPages=3

    Changed files:
    frontend/src/components/DataGrid/utils.js

    @@ -45,17 +45,20 @@
     function calculateVisibleItems(totalItems, itemsPerPage, currentPage) {
       if (totalItems === 0) {
         return { startIndex: 0, endIndex: -1, totalPages: 1 };
       }

       const totalPages = Math.ceil(totalItems / itemsPerPage);

       // Calculate range for current page
       const startIndex = (currentPage - 1) * itemsPerPage;
       // Fix: Was totalItems instead of totalItems-1
       const rawEndIndex = currentPage * itemsPerPage - 1;
       const endIndex = Math.min(totalItems, rawEndIndex);

       // Additional safety check
       if (startIndex >= totalItems) {
         return { startIndex: 0, endIndex: -1, totalPages };
       }

       return { startIndex, endIndex, totalPages };
     }

    Also updated related test cases in test/pagination.test.js

